{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tWhat is the value of the following limit?\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418c74ed2d1b3f1947d148dd6a3b7ff90a09116d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 0} (1+2x)^{ \\frac{3}{x}}\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7544808684ae304e11d9650c78e529255909d12b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ e^{2}  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ e^{3}  \\quad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ e^{6}  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"305\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tThe form of the limit reminds us of the limit definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462c3d6714b4ba8fd852647fa96402d582be80c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e = \\lim\\limits{x \\to 0} \\left( 1 + x \\right)^{ \\frac{1}{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"26\" />, suggesting that we make the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6d3b9e145e418aa7973eb0c85c5d2e2b5f64e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Then noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76a9c7714322b8986a689db59cce9238f69b5857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\to 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99d4370257071f29770e5bd7b5f22f72d7239b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t}{2} \\to 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />, we have\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d352570d26fa123637a50eb7d37ddd9c0af435.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 0} (1+2x)^{ \\frac{3}{x}} = \\lim\\limits_{ \\frac{t}{2} \\to 0} (1+t)^{ \\frac{6}{t} }.\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"34\" />\n\tSince both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8cd71a0de01efb2e87506e1e30e249bc24cf09a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+x)^{ \\frac{1}{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c572e70a011b8dc1add13d8c64eb9b08167dab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> are continuous on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, we can apply the limits to the inside to obtain\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85de2b95e4c9dad561d5fa604b02431f11cd1bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\lim\\limits_{t \\to 0} (1+t)^{ \\frac{1}{t} } \\right)^{6} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ e^{6}}.\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>\t~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the value of the limit. Taking the natural log, we use the continuity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d507b554c198a284b1e1974447663e8ab8b62e6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> on its domain to interchange the limit:\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b25956042bdff0a2214f4137049358b2e9f80ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ln L = \\ln \\left( \\lim\\limits_{x \\to 0} (1+2x)^{ \\frac{3}{x}} \\right) = \\lim\\limits_{x \\to 0} \\ln  \\left( (1+2x)^{ \\frac{3}{x}} \\right)\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"32\" />\n\tUsing the logarithm property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bbd44884f37add2e73cebabb06b1557782c726a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{b}x^{a} = a\\log_{b}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" />, we obtain\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef53cade66a050a34141ff7eacb719f35e116961.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 0} \\frac{3\\ln  \\left( 1+2x \\right)}{x}.\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\n\tSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e556591dd65d9292076018ae5b55cc7df80364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\ln (1+2(0)) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />, this limit is in the indeterminate form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d7ada08ad200c068f7060c22ead4ad2e1a2e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0}{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so we apply L'Hopital's Rule to obtain\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee462b6a60fe4829f972f511469f3e0486c19a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 0} \\frac{ \\frac{6}{1+2x} }{1} = \\frac{6}{1+2(0)} = 6.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"47\" />\n\tTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e9c412f40f115e633b865b9eaa1bb75401b679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ e^{6}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"106\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>\t~Blosp\n</p><p><br />\t\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA H